The network was built using the email exchanges of its members, where the nodes were employees and the edges were the messages. It was decided to use a directed graph defined as follows: Social network is a tuple S​N=(V,E)SN~=~(V,E), where V={v1,…,vn},n∈ℕ+V~=~\{v\_{1},\ldots,v\_{n}\},n\in\mathbb{N}\_{+} is the set of vertices and E={e1,…,eke},ke∈ℕ+E~=~\{e\_{1},\ldots,e\_{k^{e}}\},k^{e}\in\mathbb{N}\_{+} is the set of edges between them. Each vertex vi∈Vv\_{i}\in V represents an individual viev\_{i}^{e} and each edge ei​je\_{ij} corresponds to the directed social relationship from viv\_{i} to vjv\_{j}, such that E={(vi,vj,wi​j):vi∈V,vj∈V,vi=vie,vj=vjeE~=~\{(v\_{i},v\_{j},w\_{ij}):v\_{i}\in V,v\_{j}\in V,v\_{i}~=~v^{e}\_{i},v\_{j}~=~v^{e}\_{j} and wi​j∈[0,1]}w\_{ij}\in[0,1]\}. The edge weights defined according to the following formula:

